# test: profile_lifecycle
# description: Create, rename, pause, resume, logout and confirm deletion through the CLI

## Environment

config:
  name: relay
  cloud_relay: true
  tcp_port: 0
  accounts: [alice]

config:
  name: local

terminal:
  name: relay
  config: relay

terminal:
  name: T1
  config: local

terminal:
  name: Admin
  config: local
  installation: true

## Test

@relay
> amux server start --cloud --foreground
@@sleep 500

@T1
> amux login
@@contains alice@example.test  bound /

> amux profiles
@@retry 8000 100
Profiles:
  $local.id  local  alice@example.test  bound / connected

> amux profile create scratch
@@contains scratch    unbound / local

> amux --profile scratch profile delete --yes
@@contains Deleted scratch (

> amux --profile local profile rename Personal
@@contains $local.id  Personal  alice@example.test  bound /

> amux --profile Personal profile pause
$local.id  Personal  alice@example.test  paused / local

> amux --profile Personal profile resume
@@contains $local.id  Personal  alice@example.test  bound /

> amux profiles
@@retry 8000 100
Profiles:
  $local.id  Personal  alice@example.test  bound / connected

> amux --profile Personal logout
$local.id  Personal  alice@example.test  logged_out / local

> amux --profile Personal profile delete
> n
Delete Personal ($local.id) and destroy its keys, trust, agents and credentials? [y/N]: Deletion cancelled.
@@exit

> amux profiles
Profiles:
  $local.id  Personal  alice@example.test  logged_out / local

> amux --profile Personal profile delete
> y
Delete Personal ($local.id) and destroy its keys, trust, agents and credentials? [y/N]: Deleted Personal ($local.id).
@@exit

@Admin
> amux profiles
Profiles:
  No profiles. Run `amux profile create` or `amux login`.
